          "en": "**Direct answer:** In AD-related studies, reducing PINK1 expression/function is predominantly harmful—worsening amyloid, tau, Lewy-body, oxidative, inflammatory, and autophagic pathology—whereas enhancing PINK1 is largely protective, restoring mitophagy and reducing protein aggregates and cognitive deficits. However, one study reports an opposite effect on aggregation, and most evidence comes from cell and animal models rather than human AD."
