      "original_en": "**Direct answer:** Within this AD-Alterome evidence packet, mitochondrial fission is linked mainly to the **amyloid hypothesis**, the **tau hypothesis**, the **mitochondrial autophagy/mitophagy hypothesis**, and the **oxidative stress hypothesis**. The strongest direct-AD links are amyloid- and tau-related; the other hypothesis labels are largely database annotations on sentences that often lack an explicit AD context.\n\n**Amyloid hypothesis.** In aged mutant APP mice, levels of mitochondrial fission/fusion proteins were altered (PMID 35163247). In mutant APP–transfected HT22 neurons, fission-gene expression was elevated while fusion genes declined (PMID 36203194). In AD patient brains and APP-expressing models, Fis1 expression and DRP1 GTPase activity were increased (PMID 34867159). In primary mouse hippocampal neurons, mutant APP increased DRP1/FIS1 and decreased fusion, biogenesis, and mitophagy proteins (PMID 32679689). These are model/readout associations, not proof that amyloid causes fission.\n\n**Tau hypothesis.** Hyperphosphorylated tau interacting abnormally with Drp1 was reported to cause excessive fission and mitochondrial/synaptic degeneration in APP, APP/PS1, and 3xTg-AD mouse brain (PMID 29623026). This is animal-model evidence.\n\n**Mitochondrial autophagy/mitophagy hypothesis.** Several sentences couple fission with mitophagy markers: BACE1 inhibition lowered OPA1/MFN1 while raising Parkin/PINK1 and autophagosomes (PMIDs 34679674, 37016576); CEND1 reduction was reported to upregulate Drp1 and induce abnormal division in AD pathogenesis (PMID 37159984). The database assigns this hypothesis broadly, including to non-AD-context sentences (e.g., PMIDs 31614723, 34847776, 38156294), so the label is not independent support.\n\n**Oxidative stress hypothesis.** Pin1 silencing increased ROS and fission markers FIS1/DRP1 (PMID 31614723); BACE1 inhibition was suggested to protect mitochondrial dynamics against oxidative damage (PMID 37016576). Both lack an explicit AD model in the sentence.\n\n**Limitations.** Most cards (16/18) were flagged `needs_review`; several sentences (PMIDs 37141173, 33362690, 34847776, 34454008, 38156294, 37386153) do not establish an AD experiment. Hypothesis labels are retrieval annotations, not verified causal claims. No human interventional evidence linking fission to a specific AD hypothesis was identified here."
